# CODEOWNERS is the only enforcement tier that survives a compromised agent,
# because it lives in GitHub rather than the working tree.
#
# Single owner, personal repo, no second reviewer identity (decided
# 2026-08-19 -- see docs/exceptions.md E-005 and
# docs/runbooks/self-review-protocol.md). "Require review from Code Owners"
# still forces a deliberate approval click even solo; it is not a stranger's
# judgment, but it is not nothing either. Tier-2 paths below get the extra
# scrutiny defined in the self-review protocol, not a second account.

* @microbrewerGM

# THE critical protection: agent constraints and CI cannot self-modify
/.claude/                            @microbrewerGM
/.github/                            @microbrewerGM

# Rights: the manifest and the workflow that checks it are owned separately
# on purpose. data-rights must not be able to weaken its own gate.
/catalog/rights/                     @microbrewerGM
/.github/workflows/rights-gate.yml   @microbrewerGM

# Infra: laptop review, self-review protocol Tier 2
/infra/                              @microbrewerGM

# Security surface: self-review protocol Tier 2
/worker/src/security/                @microbrewerGM

# Domain paths
/pipeline/                           @microbrewerGM
/worker/                             @microbrewerGM
/catalog/                            @microbrewerGM
/tests/baselines/                    @microbrewerGM
